    "blocks": [
     {
      "t": "p",
      "text": "Investment costs can include fund management expenses, platform or account fees, brokerage, transaction charges, taxes, and bid–ask spreads. Which costs apply depends on the product, provider, transaction, and local rules. Fees reduce the money that remains invested or the return the investor keeps."
     },
     {
      "t": "h",
      "text": "Worked Example: Annual Fee"
     },
     {
      "t": "p",
      "text": "Suppose a fictional investment account has an average value of ₹20,000 and a fee equal to 1% of that value for a year. The approximate fee is ₹20,000 × 0.01 = ₹200. If the fee were 0.25%, the approximate fee would be ₹50. Actual fee calculations may differ and the example excludes taxes and other charges."
     },
     {
      "t": "p",
      "text": "Lower cost does not automatically mean a product is suitable, and a higher fee does not guarantee better performance. Compare costs alongside the product’s purpose, risks, holdings, and terms."
     }
    ]
